INSERT INTO feature VALUES('perceus-insertion','runtime','Perceus dup, drop and reuse insertion','compiled-runtime','partial','uncommon','mainstream languages','Where a precisely counted runtime duplicates, drops and reuses a value, read off the command IL''s carried supports in one visit per node: contraction dups, weakening drops, arms drop what a sibling uses, many-run bodies dup their captures on entry, and a branch rebuilding its dying scrutinee reuses its cell; a linear resident is never counted. At the emitter a closure captures exactly its support, in support order, the body''s window holding the captures in its first slots; every heap object carries a count word and frees through size lists, dup and drop stencils and the host release worklist in place; every command counts, stacks and handlers, views and folds among them: a waiting frame owns what its block consumes, a capture moves those owners and a replay copies them, a fold''s walk owns its list and an access''s frame its unwind''s names; a held cell is never freed and a view is freed when its access ends; an arm or a nominal branch that rebuilds its dying scrutinee, with nothing between that may capture the window, builds into the scrutinee''s cell when its count is one, a nominal branch of its constructor''s arity running where its match stands; windows live in a region of their own that a body''s return, or its last call, gives its window back to.','core-sequent runtime-emitter runtime-stencils','crates/core-sequent/src/ownership/tests.rs crates/runtime-emitter/src/lower.rs crates/runtime-stencils/tests/count.rs crates/runtime-stencils/tests/support.rs',NULL,'#1175');
